WEBVTT

00:01:43.270 --> 00:01:45.200
<i>You must never go near 
the castle's west tower.</i>

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:46.390
You must never go near 
the castle's west tower.

00:01:47.570 --> 00:01:48.590
Why?

00:01:51.550 --> 00:01:53.840
Because a witch lives there.

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:55.090
A witch?!

00:01:55.090 --> 00:01:55.970
A scary one?

00:01:55.970 --> 00:01:58.680
Yes, very scary.

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:01.470
So you mustn't go near it. Understand?

00:02:01.690 --> 00:02:02.480
Yeah.

00:02:02.910 --> 00:02:03.910
I understand.

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:06.670
I know what Mother said, but...

00:02:06.670 --> 00:02:10.120
Yes, I have to wonder if 
there really is a witch.

00:02:10.120 --> 00:02:13.000
Well, Alf? Is anyone watching?

00:02:13.370 --> 00:02:15.730
It's all clear. Let's go!

00:02:16.120 --> 00:02:17.240
Okay!

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:27.780
Wow...

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:29.750
It's so tall.

00:02:40.830 --> 00:02:41.890
Here it is!

00:02:42.290 --> 00:02:44.080
So this is it.

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:46.400
This is where the witch lives?

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:47.340
Yeah.

00:02:49.630 --> 00:02:51.130
Okay, let's open it.

00:02:51.130 --> 00:02:51.950
Right.

00:03:01.270 --> 00:03:04.410
H-Huh? It looks normal.

00:03:04.410 --> 00:03:06.160
Yeah, normal.

00:03:11.910 --> 00:03:14.420
Well, how boring.

00:03:14.810 --> 00:03:16.780
Since she said this was a witch's room,

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:19.730
I thought there'd be magic 
tools and stuff lying around.

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:20.930
I know.

00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:26.860
What do you think that is?

00:03:27.230 --> 00:03:29.550
Maybe it's got magic tools in it!

00:03:29.550 --> 00:03:30.940
Let's open it!

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:34.350
It's cold!

00:03:36.930 --> 00:03:38.130
What's this?

00:03:38.130 --> 00:03:40.880
Could it be... the witch's brew?

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:42.080
Is it?!

00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:43.590
It must be!

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:46.070
The potion in the book Mother read to us

00:03:46.070 --> 00:03:48.850
that allows anyone who 
drinks it to use magic!

00:03:52.550 --> 00:03:53.960
Let's start with...

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:59.160
It smells kind of sweet.

00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:03.510
It smells like it has eggs in it.

00:04:03.860 --> 00:04:05.790
L-Let's try some.

00:04:06.260 --> 00:04:07.890
You think it's safe?

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:10.520
It'll be fine... probably.

00:04:13.630 --> 00:04:15.270
H-Huh?

00:04:15.270 --> 00:04:16.740
It's not coming out.

00:04:19.610 --> 00:04:20.740
Use this!

00:04:20.740 --> 00:04:22.860
Oh, thanks.

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:33.830
It's sweet! I was right! It tastes sweet!

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:39.990
Alf, I want some, too! Let me try it!

00:04:39.990 --> 00:04:41.630
Okay, fine.

00:04:43.630 --> 00:04:45.680
What is this?! It's delicious!

00:04:49.070 --> 00:04:52.270
What are you two doing in here?

00:04:54.170 --> 00:04:56.360
The witch is back?

00:04:56.360 --> 00:04:58.270
Is she gonna kill us?!

00:04:58.850 --> 00:05:00.590
Wh-What do we do?

00:05:00.590 --> 00:05:02.830
Okay, let's defeat the witch!

00:05:07.030 --> 00:05:08.870
Auntie?!

00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:15.120
You two ate my pudding without 
permission, didn't you?

00:05:15.450 --> 00:05:16.580
Pudding?

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:19.880
I'm talking about the yellow 
dessert in that jar.

00:05:20.270 --> 00:05:23.320
So this isn't a witch's brew?

00:05:23.320 --> 00:05:25.560
Yeah, I guess it was a dessert.

00:05:26.630 --> 00:05:29.090
Don't you have anything to say?

00:05:30.500 --> 00:05:33.590
We're sorry we ate it without permission.

00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:36.840
It's all right.

00:05:37.230 --> 00:05:40.110
Now, why are you two in here?

00:05:40.110 --> 00:05:41.770
We were exploring.

00:05:41.770 --> 00:05:43.650
Why are you here, Auntie?

00:05:43.650 --> 00:05:47.610
This is my room. Why wouldn't I be here?

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:49.680
So that means...

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:51.710
You're the witch, Auntie?

00:05:51.710 --> 00:05:55.780
Yes, I am a sorceress, as well as a witch.

00:05:55.780 --> 00:05:58.470
Our aunt was a scary witch all along?

00:05:59.600 --> 00:06:02.710
Are you... gonna eat us?

00:06:03.740 --> 00:06:07.050
I would never do that. You can relax.

00:06:07.050 --> 00:06:08.470
Really?

00:06:08.470 --> 00:06:09.150
Yes.

00:06:09.150 --> 00:06:10.660
Thank goodness!

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:14.060
Do you live out here by yourself 
because you're a witch?

00:06:14.790 --> 00:06:16.960
It's not because I'm a witch.

00:06:16.960 --> 00:06:18.930
It's because I'm a half-elf.

00:06:19.790 --> 00:06:23.820
Why does being a half-elf mean you 
have to live away from everyone?

00:06:23.820 --> 00:06:28.630
Ever since the half-elf prince did 
something bad a long time ago,

00:06:28.630 --> 00:06:31.750
half-elves have been disliked by humans.

00:06:31.750 --> 00:06:34.950
That's why I live here, 
away from everyone else.

00:06:34.950 --> 00:06:38.030
But you didn't even do anything wrong.

00:06:38.030 --> 00:06:39.210
That's mean!

00:06:39.640 --> 00:06:42.460
It's all right. It means I can entrust

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:46.620
my younger brother, your father, 
with running the country

00:06:46.620 --> 00:06:49.720
while I dedicate myself 
to the study of magic.

00:06:51.770 --> 00:06:55.010
Hey, Auntie, I want to see some witch magic!

00:06:55.010 --> 00:06:56.240
Me, too!

00:06:56.640 --> 00:07:00.330
All right. Come back here tomorrow at noon.

00:07:00.330 --> 00:07:02.860
I'll show you a witch's magic.

00:07:06.350 --> 00:07:07.610
Okay!

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:13.950
<b>Western Restaurant Nekoya</b>

00:07:13.950 --> 00:07:16.950
<b>Western Restaurant Nekoya</b>

00:07:14.340 --> 00:07:15.520
This is...

00:07:15.520 --> 00:07:16.950
...a witch's...

00:07:16.950 --> 00:07:19.460
<b>Western Restaurant Nekoya</b>

00:07:17.410 --> 00:07:18.550
...magic?!

00:07:19.460 --> 00:07:21.210
It's amazing!

00:07:21.210 --> 00:07:23.300
I've never seen magic before!

00:07:23.300 --> 00:07:26.670
Today, we'll use this door 
to go to another world.

00:07:26.970 --> 00:07:28.260
Another world?!

00:07:28.260 --> 00:07:30.090
What kind of place is it?

00:07:30.520 --> 00:07:32.930
You'll find out when we get there.

00:07:40.350 --> 00:07:42.190
Welcome!

00:07:42.190 --> 00:07:46.110
Wh-What? You have children?!

00:07:48.660 --> 00:07:50.360
They are my niece and nephew.

00:07:50.790 --> 00:07:53.110
Go on, say hello.

00:07:54.300 --> 00:07:56.410
I'm... Alfred.

00:07:58.530 --> 00:08:00.120
Margarette...

00:08:02.370 --> 00:08:04.020
Nice to meet you!

00:08:04.020 --> 00:08:07.630
My name is Aletta. I'm glad you're here!

00:08:08.830 --> 00:08:10.830
Thank you for the kind welcome.

00:08:10.830 --> 00:08:12.130
Thank you.

00:08:18.060 --> 00:08:21.140
<i>I know what I'll order for the children,</i>

00:08:21.530 --> 00:08:23.810
<i>but what should I get for myself?</i>

00:08:23.810 --> 00:08:27.150
<i>I can't start with dessert in front of them.</i>

00:08:27.380 --> 00:08:30.650
<i>Is there anything with eggs and milk in it?</i>

00:08:31.600 --> 00:08:32.650
<i>I'll get this.</i>

00:08:33.330 --> 00:08:36.410
I'll have carbonara and pudding a la mode.

00:08:36.660 --> 00:08:39.700
Also, I believe this restaurant has

00:08:39.700 --> 00:08:44.240
a special meal only for children 
aged twelve and under, correct?

00:08:44.670 --> 00:08:47.250
Oh, you mean the children's lunch?

00:08:47.250 --> 00:08:51.180
Yes, the children's lunch. Can we order that?

00:08:51.180 --> 00:08:53.450
I'll go check with the master.

00:08:55.130 --> 00:08:56.340
Master!

00:08:56.340 --> 00:08:58.510
Yeah, what's up?

00:08:58.510 --> 00:09:01.450
Can we serve the children's lunch today?

00:09:01.450 --> 00:09:02.980
Sure, no problem.

00:09:02.980 --> 00:09:06.090
Oh, great! Thank you!

00:09:07.890 --> 00:09:10.240
We can serve the children's lunch.

00:09:10.240 --> 00:09:13.410
Then I'd like two children's 
lunches, as well.

00:09:13.410 --> 00:09:15.710
Okay, coming right up!

00:09:17.150 --> 00:09:19.890
This is... another world?

00:09:19.890 --> 00:09:21.400
Wow...

00:09:21.940 --> 00:09:24.430
There are no windows, 
but it's still so bright.

00:09:25.790 --> 00:09:28.130
There are so many strange things.

00:09:28.410 --> 00:09:29.290
Yeah...

00:09:35.780 --> 00:09:39.180
<i>Carbonara</i>

00:09:36.370 --> 00:09:39.180
Thank you for waiting. 
Here's your carbonara...

00:09:40.260 --> 00:09:43.350
<i>Children's Lunch</i>

00:09:41.510 --> 00:09:43.350
and children's lunches.

00:09:43.350 --> 00:09:44.950
How strange.

00:09:44.950 --> 00:09:47.830
Yeah, strange. But...

00:09:48.230 --> 00:09:49.810
It looks tasty!

00:09:50.240 --> 00:09:52.820
Auntie, what's this?

00:09:52.820 --> 00:09:54.870
The flag is just for decoration.

00:09:56.090 --> 00:09:59.890
Oh! This is the pudding 
that was in Auntie's room!

00:09:59.890 --> 00:10:02.950
You're right! It's the same 
thing we ate yesterday!

00:10:03.490 --> 00:10:04.330
No, no.

00:10:04.550 --> 00:10:07.210
You can eat the pudding after 
you finish everything else.

00:10:07.510 --> 00:10:08.830
Okay.

00:10:14.270 --> 00:10:16.840
<i>This is delicious, too.</i>

00:10:19.590 --> 00:10:21.840
Wow, it's so tender!

00:10:22.280 --> 00:10:23.730
<i>It smells great.</i>

00:10:28.270 --> 00:10:32.120
<i>It's delicious! My mouth is 
filled with the taste of meat!</i>

00:10:32.120 --> 00:10:36.180
<i>And it's mixed with the taste of sauce... 
I've never had anything like this!</i>

00:10:36.180 --> 00:10:39.200
Auntie, what is this food called?

00:10:39.200 --> 00:10:41.210
That's a Hamburg steak.

00:10:41.210 --> 00:10:44.200
It's made by forming finely ground 
meat into a patty and cooking it.

00:10:44.200 --> 00:10:47.400
Hamburg steak... It's really delicious!

00:10:49.270 --> 00:10:54.340
Is this a red tail sticking out?
 What's this one called?

00:10:54.340 --> 00:10:56.220
That's fried shrimp.

00:10:56.220 --> 00:10:59.600
It's shripe coated with 
bread crumbs and then fried.

00:11:00.090 --> 00:11:01.680
Fried shrimp!

00:11:04.340 --> 00:11:05.940
Oh, how pretty.

00:11:09.400 --> 00:11:11.690
<i>It's both crispy and tender!</i>

00:11:11.690 --> 00:11:13.690
<i>How interesting!</i>

00:11:15.850 --> 00:11:17.940
What about this, Auntie?

00:11:17.940 --> 00:11:19.410
Potato salad.

00:11:19.720 --> 00:11:22.200
It's a salad made with cobbler's tubers.

00:11:22.550 --> 00:11:24.100
Potato salad...

00:11:27.200 --> 00:11:28.960
It's a little sour,

00:11:28.960 --> 00:11:31.760
but it's really good with the 
little yellow bits in it!

00:11:35.770 --> 00:11:40.840
Auntie, this red stuff wrapped 
in eggs is delicious!

00:11:40.840 --> 00:11:43.400
That's omelette rice.

00:11:57.480 --> 00:11:59.530
You've got ketchup on your face!

00:11:59.530 --> 00:12:01.890
So do you, Alf!

00:12:06.480 --> 00:12:07.720
Auntie!

00:12:07.720 --> 00:12:09.490
May we eat the pudding now?

00:12:09.490 --> 00:12:11.440
Yes, of course.

00:12:17.230 --> 00:12:20.010
It's just as good as yesterday's!

00:12:22.720 --> 00:12:27.420
<i>If I had children, is this 
how my life would be?</i>

00:12:30.340 --> 00:12:34.490
<i>I never thought I'd come here 
and eat pudding with my family.</i>

00:12:41.440 --> 00:12:44.410
Auntie, it was all very good.

00:12:44.410 --> 00:12:47.460
Thank you for bringing us here today.

00:12:48.030 --> 00:12:52.400
You two are my precious family.

00:12:52.720 --> 00:12:54.040
Think nothing of it.

00:12:55.190 --> 00:12:57.340
So, um...

00:12:57.340 --> 00:13:01.550
Would you bring us here again someday?

00:13:01.550 --> 00:13:05.470
Yes, of course. I would 
ask the same favor of you.

00:13:07.340 --> 00:13:09.000
Yay!

00:13:16.010 --> 00:13:17.740
Another boring day...

00:13:17.740 --> 00:13:19.520
Come one, come all!

00:13:19.520 --> 00:13:20.940
What's this?

00:13:20.940 --> 00:13:23.690
We've got a specialty all the 
way from the royal capital:

00:13:23.690 --> 00:13:26.540
a stew made with knight's sauce!

00:13:26.540 --> 00:13:28.570
It's first come, first served!

00:13:28.570 --> 00:13:30.950
One bowl for just two coppers!

00:13:30.950 --> 00:13:32.700
And it's tasty!

00:13:35.180 --> 00:13:37.710
What is this white soup?

00:13:37.710 --> 00:13:40.470
It's a stew made with knight's sauce,

00:13:40.470 --> 00:13:42.800
which was invented far 
away in the royal capital.

00:13:42.800 --> 00:13:45.490
Stew? Is it any good?

00:13:45.490 --> 00:13:47.040
Unbelievably good!

00:13:47.040 --> 00:13:49.780
Better than any soup you've ever had before!

00:13:49.780 --> 00:13:51.390
Want to try a bowl?

00:13:51.390 --> 00:13:52.810
Since you're our first customer,

00:13:53.140 --> 00:13:55.540
we'll give you an extra-big helping!

00:13:55.990 --> 00:13:57.690
Well, when you put it that way...

00:13:59.560 --> 00:14:01.480
Thanks!

00:14:05.910 --> 00:14:08.490
Here you go. Careful, it's hot.

00:14:08.490 --> 00:14:09.270
Right...

00:14:15.340 --> 00:14:18.110
Wow! This is great!

00:14:18.110 --> 00:14:21.380
The soup is filled with the sweetness 
of oranie and the richness of milk,

00:14:22.170 --> 00:14:26.130
the cobbler's tubers are good and soft, 
and the meat is tender and flavorful!

00:14:26.760 --> 00:14:27.880
Another bowl!

00:14:27.880 --> 00:14:29.420
I want one, too!

00:14:29.420 --> 00:14:30.890
I'd also like one!

00:14:31.180 --> 00:14:33.260
Sure! Eat your fill!

00:14:34.230 --> 00:14:36.660
Goodness, this is delicious!

00:14:36.660 --> 00:14:38.270
So good!

00:14:38.560 --> 00:14:42.590
This stew tastes great when 
you eat it with bread, too.

00:14:42.980 --> 00:14:46.660
You dip the bread in so it 
soaks up lots of the stew.

00:14:46.980 --> 00:14:49.880
That makes the bread even softer,

00:14:49.880 --> 00:14:53.540
and when you take a bite, 
the stew in it bursts out

00:14:53.540 --> 00:14:55.890
and fills up your mouth!

00:15:01.790 --> 00:15:02.790
Oh!

00:15:05.050 --> 00:15:09.010
C'mon over and buy some bread! It's tasty!

00:15:09.010 --> 00:15:11.990
It's fantastic with that stew over there!

00:15:11.990 --> 00:15:13.760
I'd like one brown bread, please!

00:15:13.760 --> 00:15:14.690
You got it!

00:15:14.690 --> 00:15:16.060
Me, too!

00:15:21.520 --> 00:15:22.710
That's good!

00:15:27.710 --> 00:15:31.820
Today's a fun day, 
'cause it's the Day of Satur! Yeah!

00:15:32.500 --> 00:15:34.320
What're you gonna eat today?

00:15:34.320 --> 00:15:38.640
Well... since our stew sold 
out and I couldn't eat any,

00:15:38.640 --> 00:15:40.790
maybe I'll get something 
made with knight's sauce.

00:15:40.790 --> 00:15:43.080
Good idea! Let's do that!

00:15:47.340 --> 00:15:49.180
It's just a little farther.

00:15:49.180 --> 00:15:51.990
According to the halfling we met a while ago,

00:15:51.990 --> 00:15:53.730
it's in the clearing just ahead.

00:15:56.230 --> 00:15:58.640
All right, there's the door!

00:15:58.640 --> 00:16:02.100
Let's make sure it's not a 
door that anyone else uses.

00:16:02.700 --> 00:16:03.780
Yeah.

00:16:06.080 --> 00:16:09.550
They say if we enter a door used 
by lizardmen or the Red Lady,

00:16:09.550 --> 00:16:12.150
we'll be killed, after all.

00:16:12.150 --> 00:16:14.020
Anyone else around?

00:16:14.020 --> 00:16:15.940
Yeah, we're clear.

00:16:15.940 --> 00:16:20.160
The path we took here didn't look like 
it had been used by anyone else, either.

00:16:20.540 --> 00:16:23.580
And the grass in this 
clearing is pretty tall.

00:16:23.580 --> 00:16:26.500
Good. So it hasn't been used in a while.

00:16:26.500 --> 00:16:28.190
Shall we go, then?

00:16:28.190 --> 00:16:30.260
Yeah! Let's go!

00:16:36.570 --> 00:16:38.260
Welcome!

00:16:38.640 --> 00:16:40.800
Pikke-san and Pakke-san!

00:16:40.800 --> 00:16:42.690
It's been a long time!

00:16:42.690 --> 00:16:46.020
It has! What's your special today?

00:16:46.020 --> 00:16:48.400
It's cream croquettes today.

00:16:48.750 --> 00:16:50.260
Cream croquettes!

00:16:50.260 --> 00:16:52.740
They're made with knight's sauce 
and fried in bread crumbs!

00:16:53.850 --> 00:16:57.760
We'll start with two orders 
of cream croquettes, please.

00:16:57.760 --> 00:16:59.210
I'll have rice with mine.

00:16:59.210 --> 00:17:00.410
Bread for me.

00:17:00.410 --> 00:17:02.090
Coming right up!

00:17:02.090 --> 00:17:04.910
Please take a seat wherever you'd like.

00:17:08.310 --> 00:17:10.300
I can't wait! How about you, Pakke?

00:17:10.300 --> 00:17:12.710
Me neither, Pikke!

00:17:13.540 --> 00:17:15.460
They have so many different dishes.

00:17:15.460 --> 00:17:17.440
I'd love to try them all.

00:17:17.440 --> 00:17:20.500
Yeah. If only we could come here every day...

00:17:20.500 --> 00:17:22.840
Then we could eat all of them!

00:17:25.440 --> 00:17:30.360
<i>Cream Croquette</i>

00:17:25.740 --> 00:17:27.410
Thank you for waiting.

00:17:27.410 --> 00:17:29.870
Here are your cream croquettes.

00:17:33.310 --> 00:17:36.110
I'll start with the one that 
has the red spiky thing in it.

00:17:47.520 --> 00:17:48.980
It's delicious!

00:17:48.980 --> 00:17:50.630
I can taste the sea!

00:17:58.420 --> 00:18:00.240
It goes great with rice!

00:18:02.080 --> 00:18:03.390
With bread, too!

00:18:03.390 --> 00:18:06.990
What's this red stuff mixed 
in with the knight's sauce?

00:18:07.340 --> 00:18:11.400
I'm not sure. It doesn't have 
quite the same texture as fish.

00:18:11.820 --> 00:18:13.260
Excuse me!

00:18:13.260 --> 00:18:16.990
What's this red stuff 
in the cream croquettes?

00:18:18.890 --> 00:18:20.780
One moment, please.

00:18:26.290 --> 00:18:27.730
Thank you for waiting.

00:18:27.730 --> 00:18:31.840
That's crab—I mean, uh... kanzer.

00:18:32.090 --> 00:18:33.340
Kanzer?

00:18:33.340 --> 00:18:35.100
Never heard of it.

00:18:35.100 --> 00:18:36.880
What is it?

00:18:37.280 --> 00:18:38.690
It's, uh...

00:18:40.140 --> 00:18:44.890
It's a sea creature with a hard 
shell and hands like scissors.

00:18:45.110 --> 00:18:46.640
Oh!

00:18:46.880 --> 00:18:48.540
You're a big help, Kuro.

00:18:48.540 --> 00:18:49.640
It's nothing.

00:18:49.640 --> 00:18:52.060
We saw those when we went to the sea before!

00:18:52.060 --> 00:18:55.150
Yeah! So you can eat those things, huh?

00:18:55.150 --> 00:18:58.110
Next time we make stew with knight's sauce,

00:18:58.110 --> 00:19:00.810
let's try putting kanzer 
in it instead of meat!

00:19:00.810 --> 00:19:03.180
Good idea! I bet it'd be tasty!

00:19:03.180 --> 00:19:05.410
Which one should I try next?

00:19:05.410 --> 00:19:07.870
Hmm... I'm gonna try this one.

00:19:07.870 --> 00:19:09.760
Then I'll try this one.

00:19:12.790 --> 00:19:15.800
This one has smoked meat and mushrooms.

00:19:18.920 --> 00:19:23.330
<i>The knight's sauce is packed with the 
savoriness of the meat and mushrooms!</i>

00:19:24.410 --> 00:19:26.080
<i>Goes great with rice!</i>

00:19:26.410 --> 00:19:29.060
<i>This one has little yellow bits in it.</i>

00:19:32.020 --> 00:19:35.300
<i>When I bite into the yellow bits,
 sweetness bursts out!</i>

00:19:35.300 --> 00:19:39.070
<i>Together with the knight's sauce, 
it's so sweet, it's like a dessert!</i>

00:19:39.070 --> 00:19:41.070
<i>And it goes great with bread!</i>

00:19:41.990 --> 00:19:43.620
Okay, I'll have this one next.

00:19:43.620 --> 00:19:45.610
And I'll have the one you had.

00:19:47.970 --> 00:19:49.590
Aren't these great, Pakke?

00:19:49.590 --> 00:19:51.710
They really are, Pikke!

00:19:55.000 --> 00:19:56.670
You know what we gotta do now, right?

00:19:56.670 --> 00:19:57.800
Yeah!

00:19:57.800 --> 00:19:59.990
Excuse me! We'd like seconds!

00:19:59.990 --> 00:20:03.430
Two orders of cream croquettes, 
with rice and bread, please!

00:20:03.700 --> 00:20:06.180
Your order has been accepted.

00:20:06.620 --> 00:20:08.180
I can't wait!

00:20:08.180 --> 00:20:09.470
Me, neither!

00:20:10.010 --> 00:20:13.310
Here are your cream croquettes.

00:20:36.980 --> 00:20:39.300
Whew... This is bliss.

00:20:39.600 --> 00:20:41.800
I'm so full.

00:20:42.140 --> 00:20:44.480
Well, ready to leave, then?

00:20:44.480 --> 00:20:46.250
Yeah, let's.

00:20:49.610 --> 00:20:51.000
It was delicious!

00:20:51.000 --> 00:20:52.180
We'll be back!

00:20:52.530 --> 00:20:54.810
Thank you for dropping by!

00:20:55.230 --> 00:20:58.820
Weren't Pikke-san and Pakke-san amazing?

00:20:59.660 --> 00:21:03.070
I've never served so many cream croquettes.

00:21:03.070 --> 00:21:05.070
Fifteen plates each...

00:21:05.070 --> 00:21:07.570
That's thirty between the two of them!

00:21:07.920 --> 00:21:12.700
They do say that halflings can eat 
several times more than humans.

00:21:12.700 --> 00:21:17.080
That's incredible! And yet they're so small...

00:21:22.330 --> 00:21:25.410
Those cream croquettes were so good.

00:21:25.410 --> 00:21:27.780
Which one was your favorite, Pikke?

00:21:27.780 --> 00:21:29.170
Well, I think...

00:21:29.170 --> 00:21:34.190
The one with kanzer in it that 
tasted like the sea was the best!

00:21:34.190 --> 00:21:36.500
Really? Me, too!

00:21:36.500 --> 00:21:39.150
Let's go visit the sea next time, then!

00:21:39.630 --> 00:21:41.360
Think we'll find any kanzers?

00:21:41.360 --> 00:21:42.860
I bet we will!

00:21:43.110 --> 00:21:45.580
Then tomorrow morning, 
why don't we leave town

00:21:45.580 --> 00:21:48.110
and head for the port that 
lots of big ships sail from?

00:21:48.110 --> 00:21:49.370
Good idea!

00:21:49.740 --> 00:21:55.580
Oh, but then the people in town won't 
be able to eat any knight's sauce.

00:21:55.580 --> 00:21:59.540
Don't worry! The man who makes the 
brown bread taught me how to make it!

00:21:59.540 --> 00:22:02.110
Really? That's good, then!

00:23:34.930 --> 00:23:43.060
<i>Scotch Egg</i>

00:23:43.060 --> 00:23:50.250
<i>Mont Blanc</i>
